      "statusChangeID": "5e262715a301d25bc059078b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "in progress",
      "value": "In the current VRChat Open Beta, we've introduced the concept of \"Legacy Locomotion\".\nWe added in support for walk speed, run speed, jump, gravity, and \"legacy locomotion\" in PlayerAPI, accessible via Udon. \n\"Legacy Locomotion\" is a term that defines if \"stutter-stepping\" and \"wall climbing\" is possible. Let's break this down:\n    - If you're using SDK2, \"stutter-stepping\" and \"wall climbing\" will always be on. Despite it being a bug, we didn't want to break worlds that rely on this behavior.\n    - If you're using SDK3, \"stutter-stepping\" and \"wall climbing\" is off by default. You must turn on \"legacy locomotion\" in the PlayerAPI via Udon if you want to enable those behaviors.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
